        "thought_text": "Consider the parity (odd/even nature) of K and D. If K is even, Takahashi can end up at any multiple of D by alternating between adding and subtracting D. If K is odd, the final position will be X plus an odd multiple of D. Use this to determine the closest possible position to zero.",
